# A reserved word is recognized only as a COMPLETE, DELIMITED word (POSIX
# §2.4/§2.10.2). `ifx` is the single word `ifx`, not `if` glued to `x`, so
# `ifx; then a; fi` is NOT an if clause — the delimited `If` token refuses to
# match `if` as a prefix of `ifx`, and the input is a syntax error.
<<<cmd
printf 'ifx; then a; fi\n' | "$PP" run std.shell --input -
<<<assert
exit-not 0
